{
  "$comment": [
    "S3264: which ALL_FEATURES records the Wear store boundary confines to the sideload watch build.",
    "wear/config/store-boundary-policy.json (S3178) answers the question for ROUTES, COMPONENTS and",
    "PERMISSIONS; a ledger record names none of the three, so the join between the two files cannot be",
    "derived and is declared here instead. Read by scripts/quality/assert-allfeatures-sync.ps1 check 6,",
    "which requires every id below to carry wearFlavors ['noLegal'] and fails when a category named",
    "here has left the policy's noLegalOnly set - that is the moment a capability came back to the",
    "store artifact and its records have to be re-read rather than silently kept narrow.",
    "",
    "The rule the classification applies: a record is listed when the capability's WATCH half is",
    "carried by a route, component or permission the policy confines to noLegal. A record describing",
    "only phone-side rendering or phone-side robustness is not listed, even when its subject is the",
    "watch - the phone build is what 'flavors' already answers for. A phone-bridge record IS listed",
    "when the watch must participate for the capability to exist at all: every phone-watch exchange",
    "runs through .data.wear.WatchWearListenerService, which the store watch artifact does not carry,",
    "so the end-to-end capability is absent there whatever the phone build offers. Such a record keeps",
    "its SUPPORT_WEAR_COMPANION gate and carries wearFlavors beside it: the two fields answer about",
    "different modules and validate.ps1 accepts both at once.",
    "",
    "Not listed, on purpose - a capability the policy splits rather than excludes. wear.tiles is listed",
    "because all three tiles it names are noLegal-only components, but wear.shortcut-grid-tiles keeps",
    "its Programs tile in the store artifact and loses only the Sections tile, and",
    "wear.home-sections-and-view-modes keeps the home route and loses the sections that point at media.",
    "wearFlavors has no partial value, so declaring ['noLegal'] for those would trade an overclaim for",
    "an underclaim. They stay absent and are named here so the next reader knows it was a decision."
  ],
